From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 13:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 126/126] PC5: keys held at exit, taps, missing system files and free
 memory in the log

Three things a log couldn't show:

- With Keyboard & mouse, a key that stayed down in the game (Mega Man W-64)
  left no trace. The alive line now counts taps (buttons pressed and let
  go within one read of the controller), and as the game ends the log says
  which bound controls the title still holds down in it:
  "PW_WINE64 keys held at exit: l1=key 0x5a (taps=3)", or none.
- A system file a game looked for and didn't find (a runtime its own check
  wants) wasn't named. Wine patch 0986 now logs each name of a kind
  programs load that is in neither the prefix's system32 or syswow64 nor
  Wine's folder, once, for the first 64 of a process:
  "wine-ps5: not in system32: d3dx9_99.dll".
- A log that stopped while the game ran didn't say whether memory had run
  out. Once a minute: "PW_WINE64 direct memory free=11879 MiB of 12288
  MiB", the console's free direct memory as Windows is told it (Wine patch
  0914's way of asking).
